.TITLE "sort"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Sorts lines of text files. It rearranges __input data__ into a specific order based on alphabetical, numerical, or other criteria.

.DIV "ALIAS"

.DIV "TLDR"
**sort file**
Sorts the lines of a file alphabetically.
> __file__ the target path

**sort -r file**
Sorts the lines in reverse order.
> __-r__ reverse flag

**sort -n file**
Sorts the lines numerically instead of alphabetically.
> __-n__ numeric flag

**sort -u file**
Sorts the lines and removes duplicate entries from the output.
> __-u__ unique flag

**sort -k 2 file**
Sorts based on a specific column or field within the file.
> __-k__ field flag | __2__ field number

.DIV "SUMMARY"
The __sort__ command is often used in pipelines between __grep__ and __uniq__ to process and clean data. When dealing with numbers, always remember to use the __-n__ flag to avoid incorrect alphabetical ordering.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**mac:uniq** **mac:grep**

